        "provenance": "original",
        "title": {
          "en": "A letter to Ravi"
        },
        "text": {
          "en": "Meena wrote to her cousin Ravi about her school trip.\n\"Start with greeting and end with your name,\" said her teacher."
        }
      },
      {
        "id": "explain",
        "type": "explanation",
        "provenance": "original",
        "keepEnglishTerms": [
          "topic sentence",
          "greeting",
          "closing"
        ],
        "text": {
          "en": "A good paragraph has a topic sentence, supporting sentences and a closing sentence. All sentences stay on one idea.\nAn informal letter has the sender address and date, a greeting such as Dear Ravi, the body in short paragraphs, a closing like Yours lovingly and the signature.\nUse simple friendly words, and check spelling and punctuation before you finish."
        }
      },
